<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="52242" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/HIST/594/52242.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2025" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025.xml">2025</calendarYear><term id="120251" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring.xml">Spring 2025</term><subject id="HIST" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/HIST.xml">History</subject><course id="594" href="https://courses.illinois.edu/cisapp/explorer/schedule/2025/spring/HIST/594.xml">Intro Historical Writing</course></parents><sectionNumber>A  </sectionNumber><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Description: This seminar for first-year graduate students is the second half of the introductory graduate sequence. It focuses on the process of writing an original piece of historical scholarship. Topics include: developing a research strategy, locating and interpreting sources, engaging with theory and historiography, building an argument, and crafting a polished article-length essay. Students will work with the course instructor and an advisor from their own research field. Prerequisite: HIST 593</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2025-01-21Z</startDate><endDate>2025-05-07Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="DIS">Discussion/Recitation</type><start>01:00 PM</start><end>02:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>R      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>222</roomNumber><buildingName>David Kinley Hall</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Hoganson" firstName="K">Hoganson, K</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>